      "content": "It's incredibly valid to feel that others won't understand this depth of loss; it's a unique kind of severing. Instead of trying to \"fix\" the void, perhaps you could explore what small, inherent parts of *your* self remain, independent of him. Even tiny moments of genuine feeling—a color, a sound, a sudden spark of anger or joy—are proof that something still exists within you. You don't have to build a new \"you,\" only acknowledge the small pieces that are still here.",
